{"kind":"assert","text":"ARC-1 ruling on f33f0b86. The rule is yours: the archive copies one\nentry across passes, and each pass keeps its caps. The measurement\na737a945 is accepted as step 1.\n\nWhy not the other two. The bounds of the kernel do not follow from\nthe capacity of a platform service, so validation gains no bound for\nthe archive. Caps that follow from `usesPerEntry` and `entryBytes`\nmake one pass as large as the widest entry, and each later bound of\nthe kernel then moves the caps again.\n\nStep 2 is a design note before any source, because the driver\ndecides what leaves the service. The note is short and states:\n1. The progress record. It holds a position and no payload. The\n   copies stay in the retained rows of the scope. It names the\n   scope, the entry position and the entry hash, and a record that\n   names another hash is discarded.\n2. What the provider holds before the entry is published, who can\n   read it, and what happens to it when the entry never completes.\n3. The largest single stage, and the proof that it fits one pass at\n   the bounds of the kernel. A static test holds this proof, so a\n   change of a bound that breaks it fails a test.\n4. The number of passes for the widest admitted entry, as a formula\n   over the bounds. An admitted entry never answers `limit` without\n   end.\n5. Distinct sources: 128 uses from 128 sequences, and the source\n   map of 64.\n6. A restart between two stages, and a restart in a stage.\n7. The floor reads the confirmed receipt only. A partial copy is no\n   coverage.\n\nNo change of the kernel and no change of a cap. When the design\nneeds one, stop and ask.\n\nWitness of step 3: the measurement fixture becomes the regression.\nThe widest entry archives in the stated number of passes, with one\nrestart between stages, and a floor then crosses it.\n\nOrder. The note is a lane now and needs no gate. The build follows\nAE-1, because AE-1 moves the driver. The checker reviews the note\nand the build with the Security conclusion.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}